Build 1.2.4 - 2026-08-14 - CRASH, MEMORY AND AUTHOR-NAME FIXES
Cut from main @ 8259c5b. typecheck clean, 1335 tests green, build clean,
security audit 0 critical / 0 high. Capacitor versions pinned, Node 22.

WHY THIS BUILD EXISTS
This batch is complete. It carries one crash fix, two memory fixes and the
real fix for the "names show as ?" complaint. None of those should wait
behind the multi-week image and upload work that is still open.

WHAT A MEMBER WILL NOTICE

- THE FEED NO LONGER RUNS OUT OF MEMORY ON A LONG SCROLL.
  Every card ever scrolled past stayed mounted. Ten scroll-loads meant 100
  live PostCards, each with 2-3 <img>, a Radix dropdown, an
  IntersectionObserver and framer-motion nodes, and nothing was ever
  unmounted. FeedCardWindow now unmounts a card about two screens away and
  leaves a placeholder of the measured height, so scroll position never
  jumps. It fails open: if IntersectionObserver is missing, everything
  renders as before.

- A BLURRED DECORATIVE LAYER WAS DOWNLOADING 14.7 MB.
  When a post had no stored thumbnail the backdrop fell back to the full
  2560px original with loading="eager", ignoring the viewport, to blur it
  into mush. A decoded 2560x1440 bitmap is ~14.7 MB of RAM. The backdrop is
  now conditional and low priority, and the LQIP no longer falls through to
  the original.

- REACT QUERY STOPS RETAINING EVERY PAGE EVER FETCHED. maxPages: 5.

- AUTHOR NAMES AND AVATARS ARRIVE WITH THE POST.
  get_broadcast_feed returns 15 columns instead of 11 - author_name,
  author_avatar, thumbnail_urls and categories travel WITH the post. The
  migration is already applied to production; this build is the client half.
  Previously the post came from one request and the name from a second
  independent one, so "post visible, name missing" was a state the system
  could be in and the client had to invent a placeholder. It no longer can.
  The client detects the RPC shape, so it is safe against either signature.

- REALTIME TRAFFIC HALVED, AND COUNTERS CAN NO LONGER DRIFT.
  The feed-live channel had 9 unfiltered bindings on the four busiest
  tables; post_comments and post_shares are gone entirely (9 -> 5). One
  writer per field: counters come from the posts UPDATE as absolute values,
  only the per-type reaction breakdown comes from post_reactions. Mixing an
  absolute total with a +1 delta double-counted every like whenever the
  absolute landed first.

- A WEAK SIGNAL NO LONGER LOOKS LIKE AN EMPTY APP.
  The feed said "No posts yet" and drafts said "you have no drafts" when the
  real problem was a dropped request. Returning [] on error reports failure
  to React Query as a SUCCESS whose value happens to be empty, and with
  staleTime it caches as truth. Both throw now, so both retry.

- TYPING IN A COMMENT EDIT NO LONGER REVERSES THE TEXT.
  "Thanks" produced "sknaht". Two components were declared inside a render
  body, so React saw a new element type every render, unmounted the subtree,
  destroyed the <input> and returned the caret to 0. Both are hoisted, and a
  test with an EMPTY allowlist keeps them out.

- + Create posts from the top bar in the App. Blue tick shows with the name
  everywhere, including "with X". Judge scoring no longer loses in-progress
  scores.

BUILD SYSTEM
All 11 Capacitor packages are pinned, with a step that FAILS the build if a
pin did not take. This is not housekeeping: @capacitor/cli raised its Node
floor to 22 and the unpinned install broke the Android build with nobody
having changed a line of code. Node is now 22. An upgrade should be a
decision, not a date.

WHAT IS *NOT* IN THIS BUILD - do not expect it
- The Instagram-style in-app photo picker. The picker screens are unchanged.
- The image derivative pipeline. Phones still download originals, so
  bandwidth is unchanged.
- Resumable / chunked uploads. A failed multi-photo upload still orphans
  bytes in R2.

BEFORE PROMOTING TO PRODUCTION
Install the debug APK this run produces and scroll the feed hard for a few
minutes. FeedCardWindow is new hand-rolled code and a green test suite
proves a module works, not that it renders correctly. Check: no blank
cards, no scroll jump, comment typing, categories, and the contributor
score. Then promote the AAB.
